-- title:
--   Square witnesses for all nonzero Paley displacements
-- statement:
--   A literal list assigns a nonzero residue $z<2659$ to each successive nonzero displacement $d$. The recursive verifier checks
--   $$
--   z^2\equiv d\pmod{2659}
--   \quad\text{or}\quad
--   z^2\equiv-d\pmod{2659},
--   $$
--   together with the range and nonzero conditions, and advances to the next displacement. This finite witness data supports the orientation proof for every pair of distinct vertices of the $2659$-vertex Paley tournament.
-- source:
